Subject: Don't use hyphens as minus signs

Forwarded: no
Origin: vendor
Reviewed-By: Ryan Kavanagh <rak@debian.org>
Last-Updated: 2020-07-29

Tell pod not to change - into a hyphen by wrapping it in C<>; see
perlpodspec for details.
---
 doc/rxvt.7.pod | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/rxvt.7.pod b/doc/rxvt.7.pod
index 7d0a7fb..d4c4dc1 100644
--- a/doc/rxvt.7.pod
+++ b/doc/rxvt.7.pod
@@ -2038,7 +2038,7 @@ Unlike XTerm, coordinates larger than 2015 will work fine.
 
 =begin table
 
-	B<< C<h> >>	Bold/italic implies high intensity (see option B<-is>)
+	B<< C<h> >>	Bold/italic implies high intensity (see option B<C<-is>>)
 	B<< C<l> >>	Font styles have no effect on intensity (Compile styles)
 
 =end table
